  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The as-cast MgAlCuZnGd alloy has a relatively homogeneous, metastable solid-solution structure with only minor segregation.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aging transforms the initially homogeneous metastable alloy into a heterogeneous microstructure.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12806431::chunk::000::abstract::7bc48e491e",
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled aging or annealing stimulates phase separation and intermetallic precipitation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5627260::chunk::001::introduction::40d6c7eeec",
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aging produces ordered intermetallic compounds in the Mg-containing alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12806431::chunk::000::abstract::7bc48e491e",
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aging causes Mg to segregate to phase boundaries.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aging induces local chemical ordering and jagged phase boundaries.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12806431::chunk::000::abstract::7bc48e491e"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jagged phase boundaries sequester Mg.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Localized Mg enrichment promotes formation of a Mg-based oxide during high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mg-based oxide scale is stable, adherent, and protective.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mg-based oxide scale retards further high-temperature oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mg-based oxide scale improves corrosion resistance.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Without aging-induced phase evolution, the alloy forms a less protective oxide scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the as-cast baseline, aged samples will contain more detectable intermetallic phases and a more heterogeneous microstructure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12806431::chunk::000::abstract::7bc48e491e",
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the as-cast baseline, aged samples will contain localized Mg-rich regions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the as-cast baseline, aged samples will develop thinner and more stable oxide scales.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the as-cast baseline, aged samples will have lower corrosion rates and improved high-temperature oxidation performance.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The applicable aging regime permits phase evolution without excessive embrittlement.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The extent of phase evolution depends on alloy composition and aging parameters.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6197204::chunk::000::abstract::a6951d7e3c"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
